	</Specimen>
	<Specimen
		name="player-status"
		note="A stream that will not resolve; the root plays, so its status runs the real rejection path and shows the skull."
		source="packages/player/src/elements/status.ts"
	>
		<player-root class="player block" data-inventory-queue="error">
			<player-bar></player-bar>
		</player-root>
	</Specimen>
	<Specimen
		name="player-play-button loading"
		note="Loading toward playback, held there by an engine that never makes a sound. The ring on the play button appears after 400ms and the status pill stays hidden. A press cancels the load and shows Play; another brings the ring back. Emulate <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> to see the arc fade instead of rotating."
		source="packages/player/src/elements/play-button.ts"
	>
		<player-root class="player block" data-inventory-queue="loading">
			<player-bar></player-bar>
		</player-root>
	</Specimen>
	<Specimen
		name="player-panel pending"
		note="An archive that never answers, so the whole window waits: a dimmed sine drawn after 400ms, travelling one wavelength every 2.5s. Reduced motion freezes it. With a real archive each chunk replaces its own span as it lands; throttle the network and seek in the palette's panel to see that."
		source="packages/player/src/elements/panel/panel-surface.ts"
	>
		<player-root class="player block" data-inventory-queue="panel">
			<player-bar></player-bar>
		</player-root>
	</Specimen>
	<Specimen
		name="player-play-button, player-time"
		note="The parts alone, outside a bar. The first root holds the fixture Mix paused a third of the way in: play turns to Pause, and the clock counts down once pressed. The second holds nothing, so play is disabled and the clock reads <code>--:--</code>."
		source="packages/player/src/elements/"
	>
		<div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
			<player-root
				class="player flex items-center gap-4 bg-surface-900 px-4 py-2.5"
